    "intro": "Cauliflower is one of the most rewarding brassicas, but also one of the least forgiving. The curd is a tight mass of flower buds, and the plant has to make strong, uninterrupted growth before it will produce a worthwhile head. Poor soil, loose planting, drought, overcrowding or a check after transplanting can all lead to tiny button heads or blind plants. Choose summer, autumn, overwintering or mini varieties to suit the season, and give them rich, firm soil, plenty of moisture and enough space.",
